"oil_exposure":{"notes":"Indirect: BF-BOF ~21.4 GJ/t, mostly coal and coke; scrap-EAF ~2.1 GJ/t and scrap ~77% of EAF cost (China study). Oil reaches steel via bulk-carrier bunker fuel (ore and coal freight), coal prices, and gas/power for EAF and DRI. 2026: hard coking coal FOB Australia US$245/t in July, ~30% above 2025 (IEA Coal Mid-Year Update 2026); Brazil iron ore exports to China fell 2.6 Mt in Sep 2026 amid higher freight (GMK/Secex). No oil-to-steel pass-through estimate found (asked of Seb in OXH-5).","sources":["https://www.energypolicy.columbia.edu/sites/default/files/file-uploads/Steel_decarbonization_CaMRI_20210301_v1.1.pdf","https://www.globalefficiencyintel.com/chinas-steel-transformation-from-blast-furnaces-to-electric-arc-furnaces","https://www.iea.org/reports/coal-mid-year-update-2026/prices","https://gmk.center/?p=129936"]}}
